pet and padding needed to exactly cover the room?\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(0.2 inch);\n//import geometry;\ndraw((0,0)--(9,0)--(9,2)--(4,2)--(4,5)--(0,5)--(0,0));\n\nlabel(\"4 yds\",(2,5),N);\nlabel(\"3 yds\",(4,3.5),E);\nlabel(\"5 yds\",(6.5,2),N);\nlabel(\"2 yds\",(9,1),E);\n\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"5f7f9d818e9ec502511301f4345eb37a9d3e2629f1f8e5682886f6460af8c9a6"},"seconds":17.225669860839844,"seed":627421402932036473,"stop":"eos","text":"To determine the cost of the carpet and padding needed to cover the room, we first need to calculate the area of the room. The room is composed of a rectangle and a triangle. Let's break it down step by step.\n\n1. **Calculate the area of the rectangle:**\n   - The length of the rectangle is 5 yards.\n   - The width of the rectangle is 4 yards.\n   - Therefore, the area of the rectangle is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of the rectangle} = 5 \\, \\text{yd} \\times 4 \\, \\text{yd} = 20 \\, \\text{yd}^2\n     \\]\n\n2. **Calculate the area of the triangle:**\n   - The base of the triangle is 3 yards.\n   - The height of the triangle is 4 yards (the same as the width of the rectangle).\n   - The area of the triangle is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Area of the triangle} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times \\text{base} \\times \\text{height} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 3 \\, \\text{yd} \\times 4 \\, \\text{yd} = 6 \\, \\text{yd}^2\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total area of the room:**\n   - The total area is the sum of the area of the rectangle and the area of the triangle:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total area} = 20 \\, \\text{yd}^2 + 6 \\, \\text{yd}^2 = 26 \\, \\text{yd}^2\n     \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the cost of the carpet:**\n   - The cost of the carpet is $21.95 per square yard.\n   - Therefore, the cost of the carpet for 26 square yards is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Cost of the carpet} = 21.95 \\, \\text{\\$/yd}^2 \\times 26 \\, \\text{yd}^2 = 570.70 \\, \\text{\\$}\n     \\]\n\n5. **Calculate the cost of the padding:**\n   - The cost of the padding is $2.55 per square yard.\n   - Therefore, the cost of the padding for 26 square yards is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Cost of the padding} = 2.55 \\, \\text{\\$/yd}^2 \\times 26 \\, \\text{yd}^2 = 66.30 \\, \\text{\\$}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Calculate the total cost:**\n   - The total cost is the sum of the cost of the carpet and the cost of the padding:\n     \\[\n     \\text{Total cost} = 570.70 \\, \\text{\\$} + 66.30 \\, \\text{\\$} = 637.00 \\, \\text{\\$}\n     \\]\n\nTherefore, the cost of the carpet and padding needed to exactly cover the room is \\(\\boxed{637.00}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{637.00}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:410"}
